From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] engine, ui-egui: crash recovery follows Office's AutoRecover
 model

WP23 finding (owner, 2026-10-27): every start opened File > Recover with old copies, also of other documents, because the page
opened whenever any copy existed and copies were only removed by a save of the still-open document. Now: the start page opens
once for copies no earlier start has offered (an `offered` marker in the record; a newer generation removes it); File > Recover
still lists them. A clean exit (on_exit) removes the copies the window made or restored; a document replaced with no unsaved
changes (Save, then Open/New/Close in one step) releases its copy. An offered record older than 7 days is removed at
discovery; a never-offered or held record never is. on_exit also waits (10 s at most) for the docs-office history thread.
